# ============================================================================
# DEFAULT-DENY whitelist. Everything is ignored unless explicitly allowed below.
# This is the safety that stops a stray `git add -A` from publishing local drafts,
# correspondence, or notes. To make a NEW file public you MUST add a `!/<name>`
# line here on purpose — git cannot see it otherwise. Drafts/correspondence: just
# leave them out of this list (or under private/) and they can never leak.
# ============================================================================

# 1) ignore everything at the repo root
/*

# 2) but keep this file itself
!/.gitignore

# 3) and allow ONLY the curated public set:
!/ASK_AI_YOUR_QUESTION.md
!/CLINICIAN_ADVISOR_STATEMENT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/DISCLAIMER_AND_SCOPE.md
!/DRUG_HERB_INTERACTION_TABLE.md
